---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="John Morgan"
  description="Engineering leader and Fractional CTO — resume, projects, and engineering philosophy."
>
  <SiteHeader active="home" />

  <main>
    <section id="intro">
      <p>
        I build and lead engineering teams — most recently taking ManageXR's engineering org from
        3 people to 15 as Head of Engineering, after four years on Google's Search Ranking team.
        I care about shipping real things, keeping teams small and sharp, and treating security
        and compliance as a design constraint rather than an afterthought.
      </p>
      <p>
        I also do Fractional CTO and engineering advisory work through
        <a href="https://faebriel.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Faebriel</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="philosophy">
      <span class="eyebrow">Philosophy</span>
      <h2>How I think about engineering</h2>
      <p>
        Good software should feel like magic to the user and boring to maintain. Most of the risk
        in a codebase isn't the hard problem you saw coming — it's the accumulation of small,
        unowned decisions nobody revisited. I lead by staying close to the code, not above it:
        the fastest way to set engineering standards is to demonstrate them in a diff.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm an early and vocal advocate for AI-native engineering — not as a novelty, but because
        the teams that adopt it well ship faster without lowering their bar. At ManageXR I pushed
        that adoption company-wide, from engineering workflows to customer support tooling.
      </p>
      <p class="read-more"><a href="/philosophy">Read the full philosophy &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="experience">
      <span class="eyebrow">Experience</span>
      <h2>Work &amp; education</h2>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <span class="entry-title">ManageXR — Head of Engineering</span>
          <span class="entry-meta">Oct 2021 – May 2026</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Grew the engineering and QA team from 3 to 15 while ARR grew 30x. Owned architecture,
          hiring, and engineering standards; stayed hands-on across backend and Android. Led
          security and compliance company-wide (SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001) and worked directly
          with enterprise customers and partners through the sales process.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <span class="entry-title">Google — Senior Software Engineer, Tech Lead</span>
          <span class="entry-meta">2017 – 2021</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Led technical direction for a critical Search Ranking backend component, improving
          recall loss by 10%+ via large-scale ETL and feature engineering. Redesigned the deep
          neural network in the critical serving path, cutting tail latency by 15ms. Built and
          maintained testing infrastructure for a major infrastructure redesign.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="entry">
        <div class="entry-head">
          <span class="entry-title">Stanford University — B.S. Computer Science</span>
          <span class="entry-meta">Class of 2017</span>
        </div>
        <p>
          Human-Computer Interaction track. 1st place, CS Department Software Fair (disaster
          response software). Debate Society captain, 2014–2016.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p class="read-more">
        <a href="/experience">See detailed experience &amp; project write-ups &rarr;</a>
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="consulting">
      <span class="eyebrow">Consulting</span>
      <h2>Fractional CTO &amp; advisory</h2>
      <p>
        I take on a small number of Fractional CTO and engineering advisory engagements —
        technical strategy, hands-on execution, security and enterprise readiness, and team
        building for founder-led software companies.
      </p>
      <p class="read-more"><a href="/consulting">See consulting services &amp; how I can help &rarr;</a></p>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <span class="eyebrow">Contact</span>
      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <div class="links-row">
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/jnmorgan5" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/john-at-faebriel" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="mailto:john5morgan29@gmail.com">Email</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <SiteFooter showHobbies />
</Layout>
